# The build's date and commit travel in XB- control fields rather than in the
# Version field, whose one job is telling apt which of two packages is newer.
# XB- is the Debian-sanctioned prefix for extra binary-package fields, and
# they survive into the apt Packages index because apt-ftparchive copies
# unknown fields through. Required by policies/packaging-and-release-model.md,
# "Identifying a build".
email-cli: unknown-field XB-Git-Commit
email-cli: unknown-field XB-Build-Date

# The programs are deliberately fully static (EMAIL-103, owner decision
# 2026-10-16, policies/local-service-access-model.md, "How a client library is
# built and linked"): the one binary copied to another Linux distribution must
# run there with nothing installed beside it.  Static linking is the aim, and
# so is the OpenSSL, zlib and libtuikit code inside; the package declares no
# dependency because there is none.  The security updates of the embedded
# libraries arrive with a new build of this package.
email-cli: statically-linked-binary [usr/bin/*]
email-cli: embedded-library zlib [usr/bin/*]
